{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/137841-what-happens-to-relics-in-the-real-world-when-they-are-returned-to-duat","id":137841,"title":"What happens to relics in the real world when they are returned to Duat?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-15T00:00:12-07:00","id":137841,"title":"What happens to relics in the real world when they are returned to Duat?","content":"Apologies if this is covered in the books somewhere, but I can't find it for the life of me - when a Mummy returns to Duat with relics that it recovered while awake, what happens to them in the &quot;real&quot; world? Do they disappear? Or does the Mummy just take the Sekhem &quot;signature&quot; of the item back with it, leaving the physical item behind but with no further magical powers? I've got a Mage in the game I'm running who is tracking a relic that the PC's stole from him, and they are entirely unwilling to give it up or contemplate doing anything but returning it to the Judges; and I was wondering if returning it to Duat would make it disappear (thus shaking the Mage), or if it would still remain and lead the Mage right to their tomb after they go to sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1706-basileus","name":"Basileus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T15:21:19-07:00","id":138472,"title":"","content":"The sekhem drains out, and the items left over remain the same...unless they're really old, they'll fall apart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T16:35:57-07:00","id":138593,"title":"","content":"I don't know how relevant it is to your interests, but it is also possible for Mummies to awaken with a relic granted from the Judges to sort of 'borrow' while they're in their Descent. One of the book's sample SAS has a relic from Ammut which entered the world this way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}